From: Emerson Busson <emersonbusson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:15:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH v2 0/13] hv: vmbus: make rings and host-visible buffers
 survive buddy fragmentation

v1 posted 2026-09-17/18 proposed a plain vzalloc() fallback for
vmbus_alloc_ring(). Michael Kelley reviewed it on 2026-09-22 and
identified the problem: set_memory_decrypted() only works on
physically contiguous direct-mapped memory, so a vmalloc ring in an
arm64 CCA or TDX guest without a paravisor cannot be re-encrypted.
The fallback would fix ordinary guests and break confidential ones.

He asked for the opposite structure: build on Kameron Carr's
vmbus_alloc_buffer() (already upstream) rather than adding a second
allocator. This series is that rewrite.

